Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Store: permissions, startup, at runtime; AC15, AC16, AC17, supports AC25, AC62)
ADR: docs/decisions/0004-capture-store.md (modernc.org/sqlite pinned at v1.59.0)
Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md (Q10: inode check; Q11: only ENOENT or a changed inode fails the store)
Why this approach: every write goes through one unexported write(ctx, fn) that runs the inode check and then one transaction on the single writer, so T11's SaveExchange and SaveParse inherit the check. Migration uses a literal BEGIN IMMEDIATE on one sql.Conn. The DSN is built with url.URL so path characters can't leak into the query. Open takes a logger (the task's Open(dir, log)); plan.md's interface line now matches.
Alternatives rejected: treating every stat error as deleted (Q11 option a; chmod 000 would read as a deletion); recreating or reopening the database mid-run (the plan forbids it); a sql.Tx for migration (database/sql begins DEFERRED, not IMMEDIATE).
Trade-off / known limit: T10 has no public write method yet, so the tests reach write through export_test.go with an inline content insert. The identity check reads syscall.Stat_t, which is unix-only. gateway.db is also chmodded to 0600 after the pre-create so a narrow umask can't leave it unwritable. Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T10").
Verified by: make verify; go test -race ./internal/store (TestStore_MigratesFromEmpty, TestStore_Pragmas, TestStore_Permissions under umask 0022 and 0000 plus an existing 0755 dir, TestStore_OpenFailsFast unwritable_dir / file_in_place_of_dir / newer_schema, TestStore_DeletedDatabase unlinked / replaced / stat_permission_denied_not_deleted, TestStore_WriteHonoursContext); the tests first failed to build against a stub Store; with the inode check disabled, all three TestStore_DeletedDatabase subtests failed, then it was restored; CGO_ENABLED=0 go test ./internal/store passes.
